{
  "about": "What every awzy client library does with each answer the PDP can give (ADR 0045, 0114). Each library's tests run every scenario against a fake PDP: before each step the fake is set to answer /v1/access/evaluation as `evaluation` says, and /v1/access/challenge as `challenge` says; `down` refuses the connection, `hang` never answers. Each step's call is made as `principal` acting for `on_behalf_of`, a fresh client per scenario with its `options` (defaults: budget_ms 250, nothing fails open). `expect` lists the fields the result must have; `sent`, when present, is the JSON body the PDP must receive.",
  "principal": {
    "type": "ServiceAccount",
    "id": "acme-crm.renewals-bot"
  },
  "on_behalf_of": {
    "type": "Human",
    "id": "dana"
  },
  "scenarios": [
